/*
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Ottilie FULL-DEPTH PILOT — 4 samples, all 16 chromosomes, az:// on the private blob
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    A DIAGNOSTIC profile, not a contract test: this dataset has NO truth set. It exists for the
    cold-pool disk measurement and for benchmarking. The release contract test is
    `ottilie_test_az` (2 samples, 4 chromosomes, 4 SNVs + a chr I duplication).

    Usage:  tw launch <entry> -p docker,ottilie_pilot_az --config conf/disk_probe.config
            nextflow run main.nf -profile ottilie_pilot_az,docker -c conf/azure_batch.config \
                                 -c conf/disk_probe.config

    ⚠️ FOR THE DISK MEASUREMENT, ATTACH conf/disk_probe.config OR THE RUN MEASURES NOTHING.
       It logs each node's `/`, work-dir and `/mnt` usage at the start of every task. Sample the
       FIRST task on each node — that reading is the base cost and is the whole point — not only
       the peak. The probe perturbs the task hash (beforeScript lives in .command.run), so such a
       run cannot reuse, or be reused by, a cached run: `-resume` is forfeited deliberately.
    ⚠️ Launch it on a FRESHLY FORGED compute environment
       (deploy/azure/seqera-sp/13_create_compute_env.sh). New pools guarantee cold nodes, which is
       stronger than waiting for an existing pool to drain.

    ⚠️ The tool list is inherited from ottilie_common.config and is therefore IDENTICAL to the
    contract test's. Do not add tools here for a disk run: the container image set must match the
    validated 170-task run, so the difference between the two disk readings is attributable to
    data scale alone and not to a different set of containers.

    ⚠️ `outdir` is deliberately NOT set — supply a fresh dated one per run, and give the run a
    fresh work dir too. A shared outdir already produced one uncitable artifact here
    (az://aletest/seqera-runs/2026-08-07-01 mixes a Fusion and a non-Fusion run).

    ⚠️ NO fasta_fai / dict / bwa anywhere: Sarek builds them in-run and the indices were never
    staged to blob. Passing them would remove tasks from the graph and break comparability.

    ⚠️ Work dir must share the `aletest` container with these inputs under the Entra SP —
    docs/dev-practices/azure_batch_execution.md §3. A Launchpad run clones from GitHub, so edits
    here reach Platform only once committed AND pushed.

    Dataset lineage and how it differs from the 2-sample test set:
    docs/benchmarking/ottilie_xenobiotic_ale/blob_layout.md
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
*/

def az_base = System.getenv('OTTILIE_AZ_BASE') ?: 'az://aletest/ottilie/v1'

// Callers, joint-germline settings and snpeff_db are shared with every other ottilie profile.
includeConfig 'ottilie_common.config'

params {
    config_profile_name        = 'Ottilie Pilot Profile (full depth, private az:// blob)'
    config_profile_description = 'Full-depth yeast ALE pilot from az://aletest — 4 samples, all 16 chromosomes'

    // Input — the PILOT samplesheet (fastq_pilot_full/, not fastq_test/)
    input                      = "${az_base}/samplesheet_pilot_az.csv"

    // Output — TIMESTAMPED, so two launches can never publish into the same directory. publishDir
    // overwrites but never deletes, so a reused outdir silently mixes two runs' outputs; that
    // already produced one uncitable artifact (seqera-runs/2026-08-07-01). A dated literal in a
    // params file relies on someone remembering to bump it — this does not.
    // The `-pilot-` token distinguishes 4-sample full-depth output from the 2-sample contract
    // test's `yAMP-out-test-…`; the timestamp alone would keep them unique but not identifiable.
    // Override for a specific destination by setting `outdir` at launch (params-file beats config).
    // ⚠️ Evaluated when the head node parses the config, so a `-resume` publishes to a NEW
    //    directory rather than the original run's. Pass an explicit outdir when resuming.
    // ⚠️ Read the run's actual outdir from the Nextflow banner or the Platform run detail — it is
    //    not visible in the launch form, because Platform never evaluates a profile.
    outdir                     = "az://aletest/seqera-runs/yAMP-out-pilot-${new java.util.Date().format('yyyyMMdd-HHmmss')}"

    // Reference — the FULL genome. S288C_reference/, NOT the _test 4-chromosome subset.
    fasta                      = "${az_base}/S288C_reference/S288C_R64.fa"
    genbank                    = "${az_base}/S288C_reference/S288C_R64_ensembl_chrnames.gb"

    // chr_dir feeds Control-FREEC only, which is not in `tools` — prepare_genome short-circuits to
    // an empty channel when it is unset. Kept so the staging workload matches the contract test's.
    chr_dir                    = "${az_base}/S288C_reference/chromosomes"

    // Annotation cache — full-genome cache, same DB version as the contract test
    snpeff_cache               = "${az_base}/S288C_reference/snpeff_cache"

    // Mutation report — pinned rather than inherited, same reasoning as ottilie_test_az.
    generate_reports           = true

    report_gff3                = "${az_base}/S288C_reference/S288C_R64.gff3"
}
